<Legal title="Billing & refunds" description="Clear pricing, cancellation instructions and help with payment problems.">
  <h2>Cloud pricing</h2>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Charge</th><th>Renewal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cloud monthly</td><td>As shown in Recordly and checkout</td><td>Every month until cancelled</td></tr></tbody></table>
  <p>Cloud is billed monthly. Check the currency, total, taxes if applicable and renewal interval on Stripe’s checkout before subscribing. Currency-conversion or bank fees may be charged by your provider.</p>
  <h2>What Cloud includes</h2>
  <p>Unlimited cloud storage and playback bandwidth, with up to 10 GB per recording and no recording-count cap. Upload rate and abuse protections still apply. Completed recordings granted Cloud retention have no scheduled expiry. Hosted storage does not include automatic backup of editable project files.</p>
  <h2>How to cancel</h2>
  <ol><li>Sign into the Recordly account used for your purchase.</li><li>Open <strong>Manage plan</strong> and choose <strong>Manage subscription</strong>.</li><li>In Stripe’s secure portal, choose <strong>Cancel subscription</strong> and complete the confirmation. Check the displayed end date.</li></ol>
  <p>Normal cancellation stops the next renewal. Paid access continues until the current paid period ends. After that, new uploads use the Free limits. Recordings already granted paid no-expiry retention keep it, but continue to count toward storage. Signing out, uninstalling Recordly or deleting a recording does not stop a subscription.</p>
  <h2>Receipts and payment details</h2>
  <p>The same portal provides invoices and payment-method management. Recordly uses the account’s server-created Stripe customer to link billing; changing your checkout email does not move your subscription to a different Recordly account.</p>
  <h2>Refund requests</h2>
  <p>Contact support with your account email, invoice reference, transaction date and a brief explanation. Do not send a password, full card number or card security code. Tell us if a payment is duplicated, unauthorised, charged after a confirmed cancellation or related to a service problem.</p>
  <p>Refund and cancellation rights under applicable consumer law apply regardless of this policy. In particular, Australian Consumer Law guarantees cannot be excluded. We assess requests in light of those rights and the circumstances. We do not promise an automatic change-of-mind or prorated refund for unused time unless required by law or agreed with you.</p>
  <p>A refund or payment dispute can restrict new paid upload privileges while the account is reconciled. Contact support if access is incorrect. Refunding a charge and cancelling future renewals are separate actions; ask us to confirm both when that is what you want.</p>
  <h2>Billing support</h2>
  <p>If you cannot access the portal, have lost access to the purchasing account or need help with a refund, contact us using the details below. Keep your confirmation and invoices. These instructions do not limit your right to seek assistance from your bank, payment provider or consumer regulator.</p>
</Legal>
